  "notes": "West leads a heart against 4♠. The main danger on this hand is a 4-2 trump break. South has an interesting safety play available to guard against this possibility.\n\nSouth should win the heart lead and immediately duck a spade. North's remaining trumps can take care of heart or diamond forces by the defenders. The defense can cash a trick in hearts and diamonds, but South will later be able to draw trump and run dummy's clubs.\n\nIt is true that South might go down by playing this way when spades are 3-3 and clubs are 3-0. However, the odds of a 3-0 club break are far less than those of a 4-2 spade break.",
